    "result_text": "The test passes. The change is complete as a full-stack, additive implementation mirroring how clients enforce a valid email:\n\n- **Database** \u2014 `V13__contact_email_valid.sql`: new Flyway migration adding a `CHECK` constraint on `contact.email` (same `LIKE '%_@_%._%'` pattern as clients).\n- **Server** \u2014 `ContactsPost.java`: replaced the \"email is non-empty\" check with a structural email regex (mirror of the UI check), rejecting a bad email before any row or audit record is written.\n- **Front-end** \u2014 `ClientContactsPanel.tsx`: added an `isValidEmail` helper and an `emailError` state that renders `data-testid=\"contact-form-email-error\"` and blocks submission when the email is invalid \u2014 matching the clients pattern exactly.\n\n`bin/e2e` builds, starts the app, and the acceptance spec passes (bad contact email is rejected, no `contact-row-*` created).",
